      "explanation": "「李玉，你作什么？」 (Lǐ Yù, nǐ zuò shénme?) means \"Li Yu, what are you making?\". Source sentence translated in context. Pinyin keeps lexical third tones; the first of two adjacent third tones normally rises in speech. Read the whole sentence rather than translating characters one by one.",
